      "assistant_text": "According to the [[credential-scoping]] page, the Anthropic API key is **injected into the environment of the spawned child process** immediately before that process starts. \n\nSpecifically, the page describes the injection flow as follows:\n\n1. A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. The key is injected into the **environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process** immediately before that process starts\n3. The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent process receives the credential in the same way \u2014 injected into its own environment at spawn, never inherited from or written into the Hub\u0027s process environment.\n\nThis design ensures that a compromised or misbehaving Hub process cannot leak the credential simply by inspecting its own environment variables, since the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually calls the Anthropic API.",
